# ============================================================
# AGS WEBWORKS — environment variables (EXAMPLE — safe to commit)
# Copy to .env (local) or set in Vercel → Settings → Environment
# Variables. NEVER commit the real .env file to GitHub.
# ============================================================

# ---------- DATABASE (required) ----------
# Free hosted PostgreSQL from Supabase — ONE connection string works
# everywhere (your PC + Vercel):
#
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com and remember the
#      database password you choose.
#   2. In the Supabase dashboard open:  Connect → "Session pooler"
#      (host looks like aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com, port 5432)
#   3. Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your database password.
#   4. Add ?sslmode=require at the end.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.abcdefghijklmnop:MyPassword123@aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Local development without any service: leave DATABASE_URL unset — an
# embedded PostgreSQL starts automatically via `npm run dev` / `npm run
# db:push` (nothing to configure, works best on macOS/Linux).

# ---------- SCHEDULER (required in production) ----------
# Shared secret for the recurring-invoice scheduler endpoint
# (/api/maintenance/scheduler/run).
#
# On Vercel set TWO variables to the SAME random value:
#   SCHEDULER_KEY  (checked by this app)
#   CRON_SECRET    (what Vercel Cron automatically sends as a Bearer token)
#
# Generate a random string in PowerShell:
#   -join ((48..57)+(65..90)+(97..122) | Get-Random -Count 48 | % {[char]$_})
# SCHEDULER_KEY=some-long-random-string

# ---------- EMERGENCY ACCESS (owner only — optional) ----------
# If set, this single password can sign in to ANY active account even after
# personal password changes (owner "break-glass" access; never shown in the
# UI; every use is recorded in the activity log). Keep it long and private.
# DISABLE IT (leave unset) before handing the system to a client.
# EMERGENCY_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-private-password
